Inside a procedure, :PARAMETERS must be the first statement after
:PROCEDURE; one after a :DECLARE fires diag.parameters_first (error, on
the keyword).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Weigh;
	:DECLARE nTare;
	:PARAMETERS nGross;
	nTare := 5;
	:RETURN nGross - nTare;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Weigh;
	:DECLARE nTare;
	:PARAMETERS nGross;
	nTare := 5;
	:RETURN nGross - nTare;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:2-3:13 error parameters_first: ':PARAMETERS' must appear immediately after ':PROCEDURE'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:2-3:13 error parameters_first: ':PARAMETERS' must appear immediately after ':PROCEDURE'
